<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/49" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4. :fas-info-circle: [Off-topic] About AI usage and quota**
</div>

Not an issue, but I think is something worth mentioning.

So throughout the iP, I've seen the inline suggestions on how can AI help finish some certain work. I personally handrolled quite some code, which means I seldom use AI for iP. But when I did, I mostly used it for quality checking less than 5 files of the source code in one go (just enough for me), adding methods, and also for updating documentation, and the prompts are, in my opinion, quite strict and limiting ("only do X, not Y, not Z") to the point where no "obvious" token wastage occurs.

Probably the most expensive round that I did was refactoring chatbot-to-console UI methods into a new class (I've started a new thread so previous context doesn't roll the ball, and a summary of the project is provided as a Markdown file in root). But after finishing up till Level 9 (and previous extensions), I was starting to work on Level 10 GUI, and I have already drained quota for both Codex (free tier, drained at level 7) and Antigravity (previously Gemini CLI, free tier), and they're both "brand new" (never used before) which I think "isn't taken into account in the iP guide". Quota seems to only refresh after a long while.

Again, not an issue (and I haven't come up with a solution or similar yet) but I think it's worth mentioning for discussion before I consider investing in an agent. Either my perception of myself as a low AI-usage "coder" is highly distorted (if it's the case, please save me from delusion), or the issue is real.

(For those interested in my usage, you can check my fork and track additions to `CITATIONS.md` and backtrack diffs through blames.)


TLDR: Quota for Codex and Antigravity got drained before starting Level 10. I think I didn't even use that much AI. Maybe something can be done about the guide, or I am very delulu.
</panel>

