Isn't this a long `switch` VS a long string-to-function hash map? At somewhere some point the long pattern matching block must exist - I'm guessing the most we can do is (if I were to clean it up), a `switch` expression where each branch is hopefully a one-liner consisting of just a function call. Or transfer that block into a mapping ("registry"), then that makes it so that a long *method* does not exist (but something else that's not a method but is long, exists).

(Just throwing out a thought, not making a position here.)

Edit: thanks for starting this discussion, reminds me of further cleaning up iP code. Just spotted a few places deserving some cleanup.
