<div slot="header">

**6 :fas-comment:**
</div>

It should be a WSLg issue, i.e. JavaFX publishes the minimum size as a hint (via GTK) through `PMinSize` in the `WM_NORMAL_HINTS` property. But it is the window manager that is supposed to honour this hint. 

In fact, this bug has been reported since 2021 and still open and still not fixed: github.com/microsoft/wslg/issues/249

So I guess you can either use an actual Linux machine, or just run it in windows directly. 
</panel>

