As @bany-nguyen has already stated the likely issue might be that you are not running the correct JDK version, and that the fix would be to download Java 25 JDK+FX Azul distribution. I just want to add on that since you already have a JDK downloaded on your device, you may run into the issue that your JAVA_HOME and PATH are both still pointing to your older JDK model even if you have installed the correct version.

You can check which java your terminal is using by typing `which java`  into your terminal and seeing which version it outputs. If it is still pointing to the old java you will have to update your JAVA_HOME and PATH to reference the new JDK+FX Azul folder instead.
