Yes I agree with @Kia-Lok that this is in fact a cyclic dependency. However, I think the main point that the diagram was trying to teach is that just because class 2 has an association with class 1 does not mean or imply that class 1 depends on class 2, hence why there are 2 separate arrows showing the 2 **distinct** relationships. However, in this particular instance because it was explicitly stated that class 1 depends on class 2 it is correct to say that there is a cyclic dependency between the 2 classes.
</panel>

