<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/125#issuecomment-5495402926" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**18 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Hi as others have already discussed `.gitattributes` is usually recommended practice when working on team projects, and you do not have to worry about compatibility issues with your IDEs like IntelliJ, etc.

However, I think you should add `.gitattributes` as soon as possible into your project, as adding it midway through will cause one massive commit that will change all previous commits' line endings as well (I could be wrong on this). Just something to take note of.
</panel>

