### 9. LIN ..EWEI `@cewau` (9 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/25" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: W1.2d minor correction**
</div>

In Week 1 notes, under the section on [subclass constructors](https://nus-cs2103-ay2627-s1.github.io/website/schedule/week1/topics.html#subclass-constructors):

> Invocation of a superclass constructor must be the first line in the subclass constructor.

This is no longer true in Java 25, per [Oracle docs](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/language/flexible-constructor-bodies.html).

Minor nitpick, but is potentially relevant since this course uses Java 25 by default.
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/25#issuecomment-5326046942" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Thanks Prof for the quick response and amendment!

Sorry if I'm nitpicking again, but there is a further nuance to the [JEP (> _Early construction contexts_)](https://openjdk.org/jeps/513) that specifically allows uninitialized current-instance field assignment before the constructor call, which might make the provided example in the notes a bit misleading (statement highlighted in green is actually legal before the super()).
</panel>

