### 13. FOON..MING `@qqnoodle` (7 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/126" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: IP Level-10  How to design and integrate chatbot with GUI**
</div>

Facing issue in coming up with a nice design to do Level-10.
In JavaFx tutorial,  all chatbot logic seem to be encapsulated in handleInput method

```
 @FXML
 private void handleUserInput() ``{``
     String input = userInput.getText();
     String response = duke.getResponse(input);
     String commandType = duke.getCommandType();
     dialogContainer.getChildren().addAll(
             DialogBox.getUserDialog(input, userImage),
             DialogBox.getDukeDialog(response, dukeImage, commandType)
     );
     userInput.clear();
 ``}``
``` 
[link to snippet above](https://se-education.org/guides/tutorials/javaFxPart5.html)

This feels very weird because GUI itself its a big component while my Chatbot which is also a big component itself but group under a button click. 

I came up with a design which hopes to isolate the components.  
Main application starts JavaFX and loads my GUI class. 

1. GUI (accepts user inputs) 
2.  Sends Info to Main application
3. Main Applications sends info to Logic 
4. Logic Process and returns Something  to Main application
4. Sends to GUI 
5. GUI display whatever content it needs

