<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/118#issuecomment-5479942872" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**5 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Correct me if I'm wrong, but I think that not having arrow head means the navigability between the 2 classes is **unspecified**, not that there is no navigability.

Anyways, here's an example for an association between 2 classes without having a reference to the other:

'''Java
class Man ``{``
    // no reference to Dog
``}``

class Dog ``{``
    // no reference to Man
``}``

class PetShop ``{``
    void sellDog(Man man, Dog dog) ``{``
        // sells this dog to this man
    ``}``
``}``
'''

`Man` and `Dog` are associated because a `Dog` can be sold to a `Man`, but neither class store a reference to each other. The interaction is just handled in another class; but in the UML class diagram, it can be modeled as `Man --- Dog`.
</panel>

