<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/117#issuecomment-5479719616" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**6 :fas-comment:**
</div>

> I believe this touches on the Single Responsibility Principle (SRP) and Single Level of Abstraction Principle (SLAP). The `processInput` actually hides what the function actually guarantees to do, this forces the reader to check the implementation to understand what is the processing being done.
> 
> processInput might be more relevant in the case where it is used as a high-level orchestrator between the different sub-helpers(`removeWhiteSpaceFromInput`, `convertToCamelCase` and so on).

I agree with you, the proper name depends on what the function is trying to do and its level of abstraction. It should probably be an "it depends" rather than a definite good and bad.
</panel>

</panel>


