Hello! Ran into the same problems but my codex managed to figure it out. Here are the steps:

I’ve fixed the Gradle run task to use UTF-8:
run ``{``
    standardInput = System.in
    jvmArgs '-Dstdout.encoding=UTF-8', '-Dstderr.encoding=UTF-8'
``}``
In IntelliJ:
1. Stop the current :run task.
2. Click the Gradle refresh/reload button.
3. Run Tasks → application → run again.
4. Ensure Gradle JVM is set to JDK 25.
The banner now displays correctly when running Gradle from the terminal, and the project UI tests still pass. Gradle 9.6.1 supports Java 25. [Gradle compatibility](https://docs.gradle.org/current/userguide/compatibility.html)

</panel>

</panel>


