<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/16" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: 💡 Making gitmastery progress sync on work for Ubuntu 24.04**
</div>

When running `gitmastery --verbose progress sync on`, I note I had the following output:
```
INFO  You already have a fork
	Cloning into 'progress'...
warning: templates not found in /usr/share/git-core/templates
git: 'remote-https' is not a git command. See 'git --help'.
failed to run git: exit status 128

Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "main.py", line 6, in <module>
  File "app/cli.py", line 67, in start
  File "click/core.py", line 1485, in __call__
  File "click/core.py", line 1406, in main
  File "app/cli.py", line 19, in invoke
  File "click/core.py", line 1873, in invoke
  File "click/core.py", line 1873, in invoke
  File "click/core.py", line 1873, in invoke
  File "click/core.py", line 1269, in invoke
  File "click/core.py", line 824, in invoke
  File "click/decorators.py", line 34, in new_func
  File "app/hooks/in_gitmastery_root.py", line 38, in wrapper
  File "app/commands/progress/sync/on.py", line 77, in on
RuntimeError: Clone failed for progress. Your local progress has been restored.Re-run the command `gitmastery progress sync on` to try again.
```

This is due to the previous install of `snap install gh`, which has some issues as described by  the [installation page](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/docs/install_linux.md). If you are in this situation, here are the steps I took to remedy this situation:

1.  `sudo snap remove gh` to remove the old `gh` snap package.
2.  Install `gh` based on the Debian instructions.
3.  Remove the dangling snap link with `hash -d gh`
4.  You should be able to continue with the steps to sync Gitmastery with your local git client.
</panel>

