<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/27#issuecomment-5337660569" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3 :fas-comment:**
</div>

To add on, it appears you ran both the gitmastery sandbox command and manually set up the sandbox, leading to the error at the start where it said `fatal: destination path 'samplerepo-finances' already exists and is not an empty directory.` You should only do 1 (either use gitmastery, or setup manually, not both), otherwise you get conflicts like that.

After using gitmastery to setup, you don't need to clone the repo manually (that is if you're setting up the sandbox yourself). In `hp-fetch-merge`, you should be able to find the directory `samplerepo-finances` (in path `/hp-fetch-merge/samplerepo-finances`. You can `cd` to that directory to start the hands on exercise.
</panel>

