Personally I feel that having Github issues for iP might be an overkill, since it also means you have one additional thing to manage. But I sometimes pair `TODO` comments with commit messages instead. 
The `TODO` comments still act as a reminder, while the commit messages records why I chose not to touch it yet. It also gives reviewers a better understanding of the build process and why certain commits are as such. It can also provide you a chance to re-evaluate before merging your working branch into your master branch.
</panel>

