### 61. PU Y..U YU `@fireinyu` (2 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/76" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: [Discussion] Composition or Inheritance for TaskList**
</div>

For TaskList implementation, do y'all use a List&lt;Task> field or extend from ArrayList&lt;Task>?
I have seen some arguments for either approach:

Composition (List&lt;Task> field):
- Better encapsulation as you can choose to only expose selected List API

Inheritance (extends ArrayList&lt;Task>):
- technically, TaskList **is a** List of Tasks
- inheriting ArrayList methods saves me from implementing basic List API like _add(Task)_ etc.
- Up to this week's increments, I think its fine to expose the rest of the List API as a side effect for now.

I'm curious about what y'all think/ have implemented for your own IPs.

</panel>

