I implemented a JavaFX GUI for Ramly that goes beyond the basic Part 4 tutorial. It keeps the chat-style layout and FXML structure, but adds a custom gradient header, styled message bubbles, responsive resizing, scrollable conversations, and separate human and robot avatars for the user and Ramly.
The GUI supports the existing task commands, including todo, deadline, event, list, find, mark, unmark, delete, and bye. The original text-based UI is also preserved.
AI helped me scaffold the JavaFX structure, connect the GUI to the existing command-processing logic, and create the CSS styling. However, I still had to manually verify the FXML resource paths, JavaFX launcher setup, command behavior, and compatibility with the existing text UI. This was useful for speeding up development, but testing and debugging were still necessary to ensure everything worked correctly.
