### 115. ZHU ..IHAN `@zRayhhh` (1 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/102" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: 💡Ensuring Gradle project prints UTF-8 characters in terminal properly**
</div>

This is a fix for a bit of a niche issue that I ran into, regarding the terminal rendering of an ASCII banner made out of UTF-8 characters.
```
String banner = """
                █   █  █████  █      █      ███
                █   █  █      █      █     █   █
                █████  █████  █      █     █   █
                █   █  █      █      █     █   █
                █   █  █      █      █     █   █
                █   █  █████  █████  █████  ███
                """;
System.out.println(banner);
```
With ./gradlew run, this banner gets translated into a bunch of question marks when it appears in the IntelliJ terminal:
```
PS C:\Users\RH\work\2103\ip> chcp
Active code page: 437
PS C:\Users\RH\work\2103\ip> ./gradlew run

> Task :run
?   ?  ?????  ?      ?      ???
?   ?  ?      ?      ?     ?   ?
?????  ?????  ?      ?     ?   ?
?   ?  ?      ?      ?     ?   ?
?   ?  ?      ?      ?     ?   ?
?   ?  ?????  ?????  ?????  ???
```
Presumably the Gradle daemon is using some other JVM with different encoding as code page 437 should be able to display the character "█" without any issue, although by my impression the encoding used by Gradle should match that of the OS (if there is anyone who can enlighten me on how this happens please do).

Anyway, here are some possible fixes to this: 

```
System.setOut(new PrintStream(System.out, true, StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
```
This forces System.out to print in UTF-8 which somehow resolves the issue.

OR

```
tasks.named('run', JavaExec) ``{``
    systemProperty 'file.encoding', 'UTF-8'
    systemProperty 'stdout.encoding', 'UTF-8'
    systemProperty 'stderr.encoding', 'UTF-8'
``}``
```
Having this chunk in build.gradle is another way to force stdout to UTF-8.

For reference, running the .jar of the same simple print in cmd.exe yields this:
```
C:\Users\RH\work\test>chcp
Active code page: 437

C:\Users\RH\work\test>java -jar "test.jar"
█   █  █████  █      █      ███
█   █  █      █      █     █   █
█████  █████  █      █     █   █
█   █  █      █      █     █   █
█   █  █      █      █     █   █
█   █  █████  █████  █████  ███
```

</panel>

</panel>


