<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/57#issuecomment-5455449881" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Personally I also prefer to keep my TODO within the code as it is a simpler and more efficient way to signal what changes are to be made.

While feasible to have it as a Git Issue, smaller or less urgent improvements, such as refactoring command parsing out of main, may clutter the issue tracker and overshadow more immediate concerns such as bug fixes. Hence, I think it a much more elegant solution is to keep stylistic code changes within the code itself.

However, I don’t think there is necessarily a right or wrong approach. More importantly is what the team agrees upon :)
</panel>

</panel>


